*---------------------------------------------------------------
* sc.fd.equ -- the process-visible fd ABI: standard fd
* numbers (ABI FRICTION item 5) and open() access flags. Split
* out of inc/syscall.equ (task #8, docs/SELFHOST-CONVERSION.
* md phase 1) -- reference-set scan shows nearly every
* src/bin/*.s program references FD_STDIN/STDOUT/STDERR
* directly, disjoint from the kernel-internal device-fd handles
* (inc/sc.devfd.equ) and the call-number tables
* (sc.proc.equ/sc.file.equ) most of those same
* programs also need via liba/syscalls.s.
*
* `put`-only file (no code/org/dsk), same precondition
* discipline as memmap.equ -- the top-level file must `put`
* this directly.
*---------------------------------------------------------------

* -- Standard fd numbers (ABI FRICTION item 5, RULING: confirmed
* V6/Unix -- convention for the NUMBERS a process sees; the
* kernel maps them to -- MLI refnums via a per-process
* fd->refnum table in the PCB -- see -- docs/SYSCALL.md item 5,
* MLI refnums start at 1 and 0/1/2 stay -- reserved for the tty
* via that indirection, never raw MLI refnums).
FD_STDIN    equ   0
FD_STDOUT   equ   1
FD_STDERR   equ   2

* -- open() flags -- map to MLI access bits (TRM ch. 4:
* bit0=read, -- bit1=write, bit2=invisible, bit7=rename-protect
* -- READ|WRITE = $03 -- for full access). DRAFT-VALUE pending
* task #11 wiring the real -- OPEN parmlist's access byte
* through; the NUMBERS below are the -- actual MLI bit meanings,
* not placeholders.
O_RDONLY    equ   $01
O_WRONLY    equ   $02
O_RDWR      equ   $03
